{"judgments": [
 {"clause_id": "c059", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The representation that a Party \"is duly organized and validly existing, or is a citizen and resident, as applicable, and in good standing under the laws of such Party's respective jurisdiction\" cannot sensibly be applied to an individual, nor can \"duly qualified to do business.\" What Skold actually warrants here is indeterminate.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.13}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c060", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c061", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c062", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Clause (iv), \"or (iv) any other contractual or other obligations of the respective Party,\" has no verb and does not connect to the operative \"conflict with,\" \"result in a default\" or \"violate\" language. What is represented about other contractual obligations cannot be read from the words.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.18}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c063", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c064", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The warranty is given as to \"Restoraderm Intellectual Property Rights,\" a term that is never defined; Section 1.20 defines \"Restoraderm Intellectual Property.\" The scope of the litigation warranty depends on which set of rights is meant.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.18}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c065", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Skold is not aware of any facts from which it reasonably concludes\" mixes a subjective awareness test with an objective reasonableness test in one clause. Whether the warranty is breached by facts Skold knew but did not draw the conclusion from is unclear.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.18}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c066", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Skold warrants that he \"holds good title\" and has \"full and unencumbered rights\" to the Restoraderm Intellectual Property, yet Schedule 1.22 records that some of those Patent Rights had already been assigned to CollaGenex before the Effective Date. The warranty and the Schedule cannot both be literally true.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c067", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The exclusive-ownership warranty is given as to \"Restoraderm Intellectual Property Rights,\" an undefined term differing from \"Restoraderm Intellectual Property\" defined in Section 1.20. Whether the warranty extends to rights (such as trademarks) outside the 1.20 definition is exactly what is left open.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c068", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Skold's performance standard is measured by \"a physical person of similar financial strength, business experience and other relevant factors,\" a circular and unmeasurable benchmark. There is no way to determine what conduct falls below it.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c069", "issues": [
   {"issue": "A knowledge qualifier (\"to the best of Skold's knowledge\") is attached to a forward-looking assurance that use of the intellectual property \"does not and will not infringe.\" Whether Skold warranted future non-infringement at all, or only present belief, is ambiguous.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c070", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The disclaimer covers \"ANY PRODUCT OTHER SUBJECT MATTER OF THIS AGREEMENT,\" with a conjunction plainly missing, so it is unclear whether \"other subject matter\" is a separate disclaimed category. The reach of the disclaimer against the Section 5.2 warranties turns on that missing word.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c071", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The final sentence deems the Purchased Assets to be CollaGenex's Confidential Information, which cannot be squared with Section 8.5(a)(iii) requiring CollaGenex to transfer those same Purchased Assets to Skold on termination. Skold would hold, as owner, information he is bound to keep confidential and not use.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.28}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c072", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The obligation to seek confidential treatment is excused \"save to the extent inappropriate in the case of patent applications or otherwise,\" and \"or otherwise\" swallows the qualification entirely. There is no ascertainable limit on when the duty falls away.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c073", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Section 6.3 lets a Receiving Party keep \"one copy for its legal files,\" while Sections 8.5(a)(i), (b)(i) and (c)(i) allow retention of a copy \"for archival purposes or as otherwise required by law.\" The two retention rights are differently worded for the same event and cannot both be the measure.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.18}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c074", "issues": [
